{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/797819-does-knowing-of-wraiths-existence-increase-your-chances-of-becoming-one-upon-death","id":797819,"title":"does knowing of wraiths existence increase your chances of becoming one upon death?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-01T08:06:47-08:00","id":797819,"title":"does knowing of wraiths existence increase your chances of becoming one upon death?","content":"especially if you really want it.<br /> <br /> or the opposite what if you don't want to? does that guarantee you won't be one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T08:52:29-08:00","id":797835,"title":"","content":"My interpretation would be no. Becoming a Wraith requires a certain set of preconditions at the time of death.<br /> <br /> 1. You must have unfinished business that continues to drive you - that is, you must have a basis for Passions. Without Passions, you don't have a start.<br /> 2. You must not have reconciled with your Shadow while alive. That is, you have a basis for Dark Passions. A Wraith with no Shadow usually transcends almost immediately. Note that it is rare to find such people with a sense of inner peace in the World of Darkness, but it is worth considering.<br /> 3. You must not desire Oblivion, at least on some level.<br /> 4. You must be an individual with a will strong enough to defy death. Note that PC Wraiths start with five Willpower, which represents a relatively small amount of the population overall.<br /> <br /> Now, a person aware of these facts could theoretically work to make sure they come about...but as all of these represent the workings of the inner self in a very heavy way, deliberately engineering them would take some work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:02:01-08:00","id":801285,"title":"","content":"The mere knowledge of wraithly existence has jack all to do with becoming one. It might help someone who was inclined to change themselves, but that's about it. <br /> <br /> In an strange twist, though, truly desiring to not be a Wraith might keep someone from becoming one, though not necessarily in a positive way. If its a strong enough drive it might help them let go at the time of death and never manifest as a wraith. Alternately, the revulsion at becoming one of the dead could become a strong self destructive urge and pull the freshly dead straight into oblivion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:43:18-07:00","id":888297,"title":"","content":"Oh think those who know wraiths 